{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgByVyNyeYs61MWEyJzCJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The core REST module is `openmrs-module-webservices.rest`. Its `omod` (web) layer calls `EncounterService.saveEncounter` directly in three places, all for the `encounter` and `encounterprovider` resources. The `api` module has no calls. The 1.9 `EncounterResource` overrides `save`, so its `1_8` counterpart only runs for the 1.8 resource version. Each of these callers is reached through the generic CRUD `save`/`delete` path, so a behaviour change in `saveEncounter` would show up in `POST`/`POST {uuid}` on `/ws/rest/v1/encounter` and `/ws/rest/v1/encounterprovider`, and in `DELETE` on `encounterprovider`.

**Production callers (best first):**
1. `EncounterResource1_9.save` (`openmrs1_9`) overrides `save`, sets the provider back-references, then calls `saveEncounter`. This is the live path for `/ws/rest/v1/encounter` on OpenMRS 1.9–2.1.
